IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `gaa-dates`
IMPORT `gaa-rules`
IMPORT `gaa-seat`

-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 (Vic) -- worked cases for the questions of the adult for whom a guardian or
-- administrator is sought or appointed (gaa-seat.l4) and the date helpers.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The facts are illustrative.
-- The deadline rules (ss 28, 37, 152, 164, 184) are tested through their exported questions, which run the DEONTIC
-- rules by EVALTRACE inside the helper's CONSIDER ... WHEN FULFILLED (EVALTRACE ... EQUALS cannot test a breach).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases: the adult for whom a guardian or administrator is sought or appointed`

`d` MEANS `the calendar date`

`GO` MEANS `a guardianship order`
`AO` MEANS `an administration order`
`SGO` MEANS `a supportive guardianship order`
`SAO` MEANS `a supportive administration order`
`in time` MEANS `done in time`
`late` MEANS `done, but out of time`
`still open` MEANS `not done yet, and still in time`
`passed` MEANS `not done, and the time has passed`
`no limit` MEANS `no time limit under this provision`
`individual` MEANS `an individual`
`company` MEANS `a body corporate`

§§ `Dates`

#ASSERT `the days from` (`d` 1 2 2028) `to` (`d` 1 3 2028) EQUALS 29
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2026) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 31 8 2027) EQUALS `d` 29 2 2028
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 29 2 2028) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2029
#ASSERT `the date` 1 `months after` (`d` 31 1 2027) EQUALS `d` 28 2 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 6 `months after` (`d` 15 12 2026) EQUALS `d` 15 6 2027
#ASSERT `the date` 12 `months after` (`d` 1 1 2026) EQUALS `d` 1 1 2027
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`d` 29 2 2028) `to` (`d` 28 2 2029) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`d` 29 2 2028) `to` (`d` 27 2 2029) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`d` 1 3 2026) `to` (`d` 28 2 2029) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the whole years from` (`d` 1 3 2026) `to` (`d` 1 3 2029) EQUALS 3

§§ `s 3 -- disability and nearest relative`

#ASSERT `Do I have a disability` `dementia` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a disability` `a brain injury` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Do I have a disability` `none of these` EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `I have no relative aged 18 or over, so no nearest relative`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `my eldest adult nephew or niece (s 3, relative (j))`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my spouse or domestic partner (s 3, relative (a))`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my elder or eldest parent (s 3, relative (c))`
#ASSERT `Who is my nearest relative` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `my eldest adult child (s 3, relative (b))`

§§ `s 5 -- decision-making capacity`

#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: I can understand, retain, use or weigh, and communicate the decision, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 5(1), (3), (4)(e))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 5(1), (4)(a), (b))`
#ASSERT `Do I have decision-making capacity` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 5(1), (4)(a), (b))`

